WEBVTT

1
00:00:15.820 --> 00:00:18.522
On the first day of school, I had twenty pupils.

2
00:00:19.743 --> 00:00:23.765
Only three could read; none could write or do a simple sum.

3
00:00:25.066 --> 00:00:30.830
I felt degraded by my position and dismayed at the ignorance and poverty around me, but I hoped

4
00:00:30.890 --> 00:00:33.672
my attitude would improve as my students progressed.

5
00:00:34.876 --> 00:00:38.960
That evening I stood at my cottage door and asked myself one question.

6
00:00:40.201 --> 00:00:44.404
Which was better: to have surrendered to temptation and live in France as Mr.

7
00:00:44.464 --> 00:00:49.489
Rochester's mistress, or to be a schoolmistress, free and honest, in an English village?

8
00:00:50.690 --> 00:00:56.234
As I surveyed the quiet fields before my cottage, I knew I'd made the right choice, but still

9
00:00:56.314 --> 00:00:56.775
I wept.

10
00:00:57.916 --> 00:01:02.720
Mr. Rochester had loved me, and no one would ever love me like that again.

11
00:01:04.008 --> 00:01:06.029
I heard a noise and looked up to see St.

12
00:01:06.049 --> 00:01:08.190
John and his dog, Carlo, at my gate.

13
00:01:08.210 --> 00:01:13.412
"I've brought you a parcel that my sisters left for you," he announced as he approached.

14
00:01:13.432 --> 00:01:18.594
"I think it contains watercolors, pencils, and paper."

15
00:01:18.614 --> 00:01:21.275
"Oh, what a welcome gift!"

16
00:01:21.696 --> 00:01:22.436
I burst out.

17
00:01:23.676 --> 00:01:27.038
He studied my face, where I know the traces of tears remained.

18
00:01:27.058 --> 00:01:31.020
"Have you found your first day's work harder than you expected?"

19
00:01:31.360 --> 00:01:31.920
he asked.

20
00:01:33.128 --> 00:01:36.629
"On the contrary, I think in time I shall enjoy my pupils."

21
00:01:36.649 --> 00:01:42.431
"A year ago I was miserable because I thought I'd made a mistake in entering the ministry," he

22
00:01:42.471 --> 00:01:48.332
confided. "I longed for a more active life, but now I know that God has a purpose for

23
00:01:48.372 --> 00:01:50.313
me: I've resolved to be a missionary."

24
00:01:51.513 --> 00:01:57.215
Carlo barked, and I saw a beautiful young woman, dressed all in white, coming toward us.

25
00:01:58.615 --> 00:02:00.576
St. John stared at her but said nothing.

26
00:02:01.728 --> 00:02:02.529
"Good evening, Mr.

27
00:02:02.569 --> 00:02:03.989
Rivers," said the woman.

28
00:02:04.009 --> 00:02:06.991
"Your dog is friendlier than you are.

29
00:02:08.132 --> 00:02:10.353
If he could speak, he wouldn't be silent."

30
00:02:12.314 --> 00:02:17.136
St. John flushed; he looked at the ground and crushed some flower buds underneath his foot.

31
00:02:17.156 --> 00:02:20.078
"Did I furnish your cottage nicely?"

32
00:02:20.478 --> 00:02:21.099
she asked me.

33
00:02:21.119 --> 00:02:23.600
"Very nicely indeed."

34
00:02:24.801 --> 00:02:27.822
I realized that this beauty was Rosamond Oliver.

35
00:02:29.023 --> 00:02:30.464
She turned her attention to St.

36
00:02:30.484 --> 00:02:30.964
John again.

37
00:02:32.224 --> 00:02:34.346
"Papa is alone this evening and not well.

38
00:02:35.587 --> 00:02:37.309
Won't you return with me and visit him?"

39
00:02:38.530 --> 00:02:39.911
"Not tonight, Miss Rosamond.

40
00:02:41.092 --> 00:02:42.193
It's too late for a visit."

41
00:02:43.374 --> 00:02:44.876
St. John spoke mechanically.

42
00:02:46.077 --> 00:02:50.821
But I could hear in his low, hollow voice how painful it was for him to refuse her.

43
00:02:50.841 --> 00:02:54.825
"Well, then I shall be going," she said to him.

44
00:02:54.845 --> 00:02:58.248
"I'll visit the schoolroom," she promised me.

45
00:02:59.400 --> 00:03:04.004
As the months passed, my pupils began to make progress, and I felt that I was becoming a

46
00:03:04.104 --> 00:03:05.346
favorite in the neighborhood.

47
00:03:07.287 --> 00:03:12.212
At this point I was happy more often than not, and yet in the midst of this calm,

48
00:03:12.652 --> 00:03:13.913
I kept dreaming of Mr.

49
00:03:13.973 --> 00:03:20.139
Rochester. I would awake in the middle of the night, realize where I was, and be filled with

50
00:03:20.199 --> 00:03:25.664
despair. But every morning I calmly opened the school and greeted my pupils.

51
00:03:26.868 --> 00:03:29.449
Miss Oliver kept her word about coming to the school.

52
00:03:30.729 --> 00:03:33.590
She generally made her visit in the course of her morning ride.

53
00:03:34.790 --> 00:03:40.972
In her purple riding habit and black velvet cap, she would enter the rustic building and glide through

54
00:03:40.992 --> 00:03:43.093
the dazzled ranks of the village children.

55
00:03:44.413 --> 00:03:45.733
She often arrived when St.

56
00:03:45.753 --> 00:03:47.754
John was giving his daily Bible lesson.

57
00:03:48.954 --> 00:03:54.456
As she gave him a smile, his hands would tremble and his cheeks would burn, but he didn't

58
00:03:54.516 --> 00:03:55.456
return her smile.

59
00:03:56.776 --> 00:04:00.177
Miss Oliver also honored me with frequent visits to my cottage.

60
00:04:02.118 --> 00:04:05.299
Indulged from birth, she was very different from St.

61
00:04:05.319 --> 00:04:06.059
John's sisters.

62
00:04:07.479 --> 00:04:10.620
Still, I liked her almost as much as I liked Adele.

63
00:04:11.921 --> 00:04:16.902
One evening while rummaging through my cupboard, she discovered my drawing materials and some sketches.

64
00:04:16.922 --> 00:04:20.143
"Would you make a portrait of me for Papa?"

65
00:04:20.563 --> 00:04:21.163
she asked.

66
00:04:22.404 --> 00:04:23.104
"With pleasure."

67
00:04:24.368 --> 00:04:27.630
I was thrilled at the idea of capturing such a perfect subject.

68
00:04:28.831 --> 00:04:32.454
I took a sheet of fine cardboard and drew a careful outline.

69
00:04:33.695 --> 00:04:38.578
As it was late in the day, I promised myself the pleasure of coloring the picture another time.

70
00:04:39.759 --> 00:04:45.463
A few days later it was a holiday, so I devoted that November afternoon to completing the portrait.

71
00:04:46.744 --> 00:04:50.927
I was absorbed in the finishing touches when, after one quick knock, St.

72
00:04:50.947 --> 00:04:52.148
John entered my cottage.

73
00:04:53.404 --> 00:04:54.965
"I've brought you a new book of poetry."

74
00:04:56.146 --> 00:04:57.186
He handed me the book.

75
00:04:59.107 --> 00:05:01.749
While I eagerly glanced at the poetry, St.

76
00:05:01.769 --> 00:05:07.352
John stooped to examine my drawing, but startled by its subject, he immediately stood upright.

77
00:05:07.372 --> 00:05:10.193
"Is this portrait a good resemblance?"

78
00:05:10.613 --> 00:05:11.414
I asked bluntly.

79
00:05:11.434 --> 00:05:15.276
"A well-executed picture," he responded.

80
00:05:15.296 --> 00:05:18.137
"Very graceful and correct drawing."

81
00:05:18.157 --> 00:05:20.919
"But what of the resemblance?

82
00:05:22.099 --> 00:05:22.940
Who does it look like?"

83
00:05:24.164 --> 00:05:28.987
After some hesitation, he said, "Miss Oliver, I presume."

84
00:05:29.007 --> 00:05:32.029
"I'll paint a copy for you, if you like.

85
00:05:33.230 --> 00:05:37.273
Would it comfort you or torment you to have such a painting with you when you're a missionary?"

86
00:05:38.514 --> 00:05:40.395
He glanced at me and then at the picture.

87
00:05:40.415 --> 00:05:45.598
"I would certainly like to have it, but whether that would be wise is another question."

88
00:05:45.619 --> 00:05:49.701
"She likes you, I'm sure," I said.

89
00:05:49.721 --> 00:05:51.803
"You ought to marry her."

90
00:05:51.823 --> 00:05:53.604
"Does she like me?"

91
00:05:53.928 --> 00:05:54.949
He seemed startled.

92
00:05:54.969 --> 00:06:03.492
"Certainly. She talks of you constantly; there's no subject she enjoys so much or touches upon so often."

93
00:06:03.512 --> 00:06:09.915
"It's strange," he said, "that while I love her wildly, I know that she's not the partner for

94
00:06:09.955 --> 00:06:12.816
me. Rosamond a missionary's wife?

95
00:06:13.916 --> 00:06:17.078
Never!" "But you don't have to be a missionary.

96
00:06:18.158 --> 00:06:19.879
You could relinquish that scheme."

97
00:06:19.899 --> 00:06:22.400
"Relinquish my vocation?

98
00:06:23.656 --> 00:06:25.677
My work is dearer to me than my own blood."

99
00:06:26.858 --> 00:06:30.640
After a considerable pause, I said, "But what about Miss Oliver?

100
00:06:31.821 --> 00:06:34.442
Are her disappointment and sorrow of no interest to you?"

101
00:06:35.623 --> 00:06:37.604
"Miss Oliver is always surrounded by suitors.

102
00:06:38.825 --> 00:06:41.206
In less than a month, she'll forget me and marry someone else."

103
00:06:41.226 --> 00:06:47.810
"You speak coolly enough, but you tremble and flush whenever she enters the schoolroom."

104
00:06:48.971 --> 00:06:50.952
"And you are quite bold and original."

105
00:06:52.020 --> 00:06:55.383
He picked up his hat, which lay on the table beside my palette.

106
00:06:56.543 --> 00:06:58.044
Once more he looked at the picture.

107
00:06:59.265 --> 00:07:01.247
"She is lovely," he murmured.

108
00:07:01.267 --> 00:07:03.929
"So may I paint a copy for you?"

109
00:07:05.090 --> 00:07:09.833
"No." He was about to cover the portrait with the thin sheet of paper that I used to

110
00:07:09.873 --> 00:07:12.535
keep it clean when he suddenly spotted something.

111
00:07:13.776 --> 00:07:14.877
He shot a glance at me.

112
00:07:14.897 --> 00:07:16.738
"What's the matter?"

113
00:07:17.098 --> 00:07:17.579
I asked.

114
00:07:18.920 --> 00:07:24.746
"Nothing." But as he replaced the paper, I saw him tear a narrow piece from the edge.

115
00:07:24.966 --> 00:07:29.607
It disappeared into his glove, and with a hasty nod and a quick good-bye, he vanished.

116
00:07:30.848 --> 00:07:35.830
I studied the paper, but could see nothing except a few paint stains, so I soon forgot his

117
00:07:35.870 --> 00:07:36.750
strange behavior.
